  'Interfax and TASS in English relay the words of Lithuanian Prime Minister Mindaugas Sinkevicius after a meeting of the National Security Commission: the drone that violated the country\'s airspace on 18 October was Ukrainian, carried explosives and crossed the border from the Polish side; Lithuanian radars, unlike Polish ones, recorded the moment, and the Ukrainian side confirmed it had lost contact with one of its drones. RIA Novosti adds that Lithuania will consult NATO to obtain the right to shoot down drones without visual confirmation, and writes that the Baltic states "allegedly" did not give Ukraine permission to use their airspace. The next day Interfax reported that Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk expects a full explanation from Ukraine and stressed that Poland does not allow operations over its territory without its consent, while Lithuanian President Gitanas Nauseda said the defence ministries of Lithuania and Poland had set up a joint working group to investigate.',
